WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.203
-So, guys, we are smack in
the middle of March Madness.

00:00:03.203 --> 00:00:05.638
And every year, we pick a team
to root for,

00:00:05.638 --> 00:00:08.174
and this year,
we picked Gonzaga, okay?

00:00:08.174 --> 00:00:11.077
So we gave out these rowdy rags

00:00:11.077 --> 00:00:13.779
to all the students that are
following the team around, okay?

00:00:13.779 --> 00:00:16.349
And what we want them to do is,
at a certain point,

00:00:16.349 --> 00:00:17.883
just stand up
and start whipping them around

00:00:17.883 --> 00:00:19.518
and do something, you know,
something crazy.

00:00:19.518 --> 00:00:22.922
And so far, it's worked.
They've won the last two games.

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:24.524
-Ooh.
-Yeah.

00:00:24.524 --> 00:00:26.726
I'm just saying.

00:00:26.726 --> 00:00:28.695
They were nail-biters,
but they did win.

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:30.096
-Yes.
-Yeah, so now they're playing

00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:31.264
tomorrow.

00:00:31.264 --> 00:00:33.333
They're playing
the Arkansas Razorbacks.

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:34.900
-Uh-oh.
[ Light cheering ]

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:36.870
-No. No.

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:39.004
We have to -- We have to --

00:00:39.004 --> 00:00:40.606
I mean, I love them,
I hope they do well.

00:00:40.606 --> 00:00:43.209
-Yeah, but not too well.
-Not too well, yeah, exactly.

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:45.745
We want to help Gonzaga
win again, okay?

00:00:45.745 --> 00:00:47.247
But I think we should
switch it up.

00:00:47.247 --> 00:00:49.515
'Cause right now,
we want 'em to sing like,

00:00:49.515 --> 00:00:51.417
"I'll tell you what I want,
what I really really want."

00:00:51.417 --> 00:00:53.252
Yeah, I'm changing that up.
-What?

00:00:53.252 --> 00:00:54.420
-Basically,
here's what we want them to do.

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:56.189
Each half is 20 minutes, right?

00:00:56.189 --> 00:00:58.958
So when the game clock
goes down to 11:35 --

00:00:58.958 --> 00:01:01.027
that's when
"The Tonight Show" airs --

00:01:01.027 --> 00:01:03.429
I want everyone to stand up

00:01:03.429 --> 00:01:06.399
and just take their rowdy rags
and whip it around.

00:01:06.399 --> 00:01:09.368
But I want to -- Since they're
playing the Arkansas Razorbacks,

00:01:09.368 --> 00:01:11.103
I think they should go...

00:01:11.103 --> 00:01:13.239
♪ Let's beat the Razorbacks,
Razorbacks, Razorbacks ♪

00:01:13.306 --> 00:01:15.641
♪ Let's beat the Razorbacks,
Razorbacks, Razorbacks ♪

00:01:15.641 --> 00:01:19.445
♪ We'll beat
the Razorback kids ♪

00:01:19.445 --> 00:01:22.848
♪ Beat the Razorback kids ♪

00:01:22.848 --> 00:01:24.817
♪ Beat Arkansas ♪

00:01:24.817 --> 00:01:27.153
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:28.454 --> 00:01:30.890
You're laughing.
What are you laughing at?

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:32.825
-That seems like a lot.
-Wait, wait.

00:01:32.825 --> 00:01:34.294
You think that the students --

00:01:34.294 --> 00:01:36.795
-And the harmonies? You want 'em
to get the harmonies in there?

00:01:36.795 --> 00:01:39.398
-You think the kids
won't stand up at 11:35 --

00:01:39.398 --> 00:01:41.968
-Oh, no. They will.
I'm not saying they won't.

00:01:41.968 --> 00:01:44.070
But I don't think
it'll sound like that.

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:45.671
[ Laughter ]

00:01:45.671 --> 00:01:47.140
-It might be too tricky.

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:49.742
So at 11:20 -- 11:35...
-11:35.

00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:51.311
-...definitely 11:35 --

00:01:51.311 --> 00:01:54.981
stand up, and what I would like
you to try, again, if we can --

00:01:54.981 --> 00:01:57.050
Can we see if we can do it?

00:01:57.050 --> 00:01:59.285
All right. And the Arkansas fan,
you don't have to do it.

00:01:59.285 --> 00:02:02.255
You can sit in quiet protest.

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:05.057
One, two...

00:02:05.057 --> 00:02:07.059
♪ Let's beat the Razorbacks,
Razorbacks, Razorbacks ♪

00:02:07.126 --> 00:02:09.562
♪ Let's beat the Razorbacks,
Razorbacks, Razorbacks ♪

00:02:09.562 --> 00:02:13.266
♪ We'll beat
the Razorback kids ♪

00:02:13.266 --> 00:02:15.868
Stop. Just stop, stop,
stop, stop, stop.

00:02:15.868 --> 00:02:17.136
Absolutely no.

00:02:17.136 --> 00:02:19.105
It's a disaster.

00:02:19.105 --> 00:02:20.973
It's a complete disaster.
-Well, it's a high harmony.

00:02:20.973 --> 00:02:22.975
-It's a complete disaster.
-Get rid of that high harmony.

00:02:22.975 --> 00:02:25.044
-They're never going to do it.
-Right.

00:02:25.044 --> 00:02:26.946
And somebody's gonna have to
yell, "One, two, three."

00:02:26.946 --> 00:02:28.914
You know what I mean?
-That's it?

00:02:28.914 --> 00:02:30.916
-Well, just go -- Yeah.
-Oh, that's pretty good.

00:02:30.916 --> 00:02:32.684
They'll have to stand up and go,
"One, two, three,"

00:02:32.684 --> 00:02:34.387
and don't say anything.
-Yeah.

00:02:34.387 --> 00:02:35.921
[ Laughter ]

00:02:35.921 --> 00:02:38.190
-Yeah. And then quiet.
-Right.

00:02:38.190 --> 00:02:39.959
-All right, so at 11:35 --
I'm changing it up.

00:02:39.959 --> 00:02:42.962
I'm changing it up.
-Boom. So at 11:35 -- 11:34.

00:02:42.962 --> 00:02:44.764
-So when it goes down
to 11:40 tonight --

00:02:44.764 --> 00:02:49.635
Oh, here it comes down to
11:37, 11:36, 11:35,

00:02:49.635 --> 00:02:52.337
you go, "One, two, three!"
-Boom.

00:02:52.337 --> 00:02:55.141
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:57.076 --> 00:02:59.512
-Okay. That's what they'll do.
-There you go.

00:02:59.512 --> 00:03:02.848
-Forget about the other one.
It's too confusing. I apologize.

00:03:02.848 --> 00:03:04.817
I apologize. That was --
Yeah, why would --

00:03:04.817 --> 00:03:06.986
-It was good heart.
-It's tomorrow night.

00:03:06.986 --> 00:03:08.287
It's tomorrow night
they're playing.

00:03:08.287 --> 00:03:09.488
-What time?

00:03:09.488 --> 00:03:10.924
-You got to check
your local listings.

00:03:10.924 --> 00:03:12.257
-Okay.

00:03:12.257 --> 00:03:14.426
-I think tomorrow --
Do we know what time they play?

00:03:14.426 --> 00:03:15.961
-7:00.
-7:00

00:03:15.961 --> 00:03:17.530
on the dot.
-Ooh.

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:19.365
-But "at 7:00"
doesn't mean anything to me,

00:03:19.365 --> 00:03:22.268
'cause it's when the clock
goes down to 11:35 --

00:03:22.268 --> 00:03:23.769
-Each...?
-Each half.

00:03:23.769 --> 00:03:24.804
-Yes.
-You got two opportunities.

00:03:24.804 --> 00:03:25.805
for the students.

00:03:25.805 --> 00:03:27.373
If you're rooting
for your team --

00:03:27.373 --> 00:03:29.809
Gonzaga -- if you're rooting
for the Bulldogs,

00:03:29.809 --> 00:03:32.011
I want you to go...

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:34.680
at 11:36, 11:35,

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:37.216
"One, two, three!"

00:03:37.216 --> 00:03:39.552
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:39.552 --> 00:03:41.153
-Hey...

00:03:41.153 --> 00:03:43.622
-Look at your phone.
-Yeah, look at your phone.

00:03:43.622 --> 00:03:45.290
-Look at your phone or
something, do whatever you want.

00:03:45.290 --> 00:03:46.693
-Check your message, like,
check for your keys.

00:03:46.693 --> 00:03:48.728
-Yeah. Yeah, exactly.
That's what I want.

00:03:48.728 --> 00:03:50.362
-And then imaginarily
talk to somebody.

00:03:50.362 --> 00:03:51.930
-And go Zags.
Go Zags, everybody.

00:03:51.930 --> 00:03:53.666
We got this. Come on.

00:03:53.666 --> 00:03:55.335
We got this.
Sweet 16, baby.

